qnx_gles2_bench: driver control 0: INFINITE_FAST_DRIVER Driver returns after very minimal work. Useful when you want to profile the performance of your app with no GPU or driver CPU overhead. It is unsafe to disable this mode after it has been enabled because the driver is in an undefined state and none of the GL objects will have been created.
qnx_gles2_bench: driver control 1: INFINITE_FAST_HARDWARE Driver does all error checking and command buffer generation, but the command buffer is not sent to the GPU. Useful when you want to profile CPU performance of your app and the driver with no GPU overhead. It is unsafe to disable this mode after it has been enabled because none of the GL objects will have been created.
